WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
Yoga classes, talk of
karma, Diwali lights:

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.380
Hindu words and pictures
are everywhere in Britain.

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.900
About a million people in England and
Wales now tell the Census they are Hindu.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.920
Their families speak Gujarati, Punjabi,
Tamil and many other languages.

5
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.810
So does the West really
understand Hinduism,

6
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.400
or only borrow its words and pictures?

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.700
And what does it mean to grow
up Hindu in Britain today?

8
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.550
In this mission, you'll ask whether
British Hindus share one clear identity.

9
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.360
Then you'll ask what makes
someone a British Hindu,

10
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.350
across three generations.

11
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.800
Your mission: find out how
the West sees Hinduism,

12
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.330
and what being a British
Hindu means today.
